{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ContentSumNStatistic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ContentSumNStatistic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneModularTwist","lean:module:QOU.Common.HookSumComplete"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ContentSumNStatistic.contentSum_eq_hookSum_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ContentSumNStatistic.contentSum_eq_hookSum_sub","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ContentSumNStatistic.lean#L105-L120","doc":"**The n-statistic identity** `κ_λ = Σ_x h_x − |λ| − 2·n(λ)`, in the `Partition.hookLength`\nencoding used by `hookProd`/`schurElement` — the exponent identity the telescope-closure convention\nbridge `hconv` turns on (audit `docs/audits/2026-08-29-normalizedsum-closes-via-telescope.md`).\nCombines `contentSum_eq_nLambda_conj_sub` (`κ = n(λ') − n(λ)`) with the hook-sum identity\n`Σ_x h_x = n(λ') + n(λ) + |λ|` (`HookSumComplete.hookSum_eq`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ContentSumNStatistic.partitionHookSum_eq_hookSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ContentSumNStatistic.partitionHookSum_eq_hookSum","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ContentSumNStatistic.lean#L89-L103","doc":"The genuine-cell hook sum `Σ_x Partition.hookLength` equals `HookSumComplete.hookSum` (the\n`colLen`-hook), cell by cell (`IdentityI.hookLength_eq` + the arm/leg `≥ 1` bounds from\n`colLen_duality`, and the `colLen` bridge). Bridges the `Partition.hookLength` encoding (used by\n`hookProd`/`schurElement`) to the register in which the hook-sum identity is proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ContentSumNStatistic.colSum_headD_eq_nLambda_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ContentSumNStatistic.colSum_headD_eq_nLambda_conj","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ContentSumNStatistic.lean#L80-L87","doc":"`colSum λ (max part) = n(λ')`: the column sum `Σ_j (colLen j)·j` is `n(λ') = nLambda (conj λ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ContentSumNStatistic.bStat_eq_nLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ContentSumNStatistic.bStat_eq_nLambda","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ContentSumNStatistic.lean#L74-L78","doc":"`bStat λ = n(λ)`: the two `Σ_i i·λ_i` encodings agree (`l.getD i 0 = (l[i]?).getD 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ContentSumNStatistic.hsc_colLen_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ContentSumNStatistic.hsc_colLen_eq","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ContentSumNStatistic.lean#L59-L72","doc":"**The two `colLen` encodings agree.** `HookSumComplete.colLen` counts *row indices* `i` with\n`λ_i > j` (a `Finset.range` card), while `IdentityI.colLen` filters the *list values* `> j`; both\ncount `#{cells in column j}`. Bridges the self-contained `HookSumComplete` register (in which the\nhook-sum identity `hookSum_eq` is proved) to the `IdentityI`/`conj` register everything else uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ContentSumNStatistic.contentSum_eq_nLambda_conj_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ContentSumNStatistic.contentSum_eq_nLambda_conj_sub","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ContentSumNStatistic.lean#L32-L57","doc":"**`contentSum λ = n(λ') − n(λ)`** (the conjugate/`n`-statistic form of the content sum), for a\nweakly-decreasing partition `λ`. The content of a cell `(i,j)` is `j − i`; summing the `j`-part by\ncolumns gives `n(λ') = nLambda (conj λ)` and the `i`-part by rows gives `n(λ) = nLambda λ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}